# Environment
#
# Default-deny, because the file that leaks is never the one a rule was written for: a copy
# of .env taken before a risky change (.env.bak.pre-bifrost, .env.old, .env.2026-09-12) holds
# exactly the same credentials and is named whatever the person was thinking at the time. An
# allowlist of backup suffixes would only ever cover the shapes somebody already met.
#
# The negations name the env files that are meant to be committed — they carry no secrets.
# Listing one here is the decision to publish it, so a new one must be added deliberately.
#
# Each negation is ANCHORED to its full path, for the reason the worker-binary block above
# records in the other direction: a pattern with no slash in it matches that name at ANY
# depth. Unanchored, `!.env.example` would also re-admit a `.env.example` nobody has written
# yet, in a directory nobody has created yet — and `!.env.production` would re-admit a
# future service's production env, which is the one file in this whole block most likely to
# hold a live credential. Default-deny only holds if the exceptions cannot spread.
.env
.env.*
!/.env.example
!/web/.env.example
!/extension/.env.production

# IDE / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Agent tooling local state. `.claude/` and `.codex/` are per-machine configuration for
# the harnesses agents run under — the same class of file as an editor's local settings —
# and `skills-lock.json` is what they install. None of that belongs in the tree: the
# shared rules live in AGENTS.md, which IS committed.
#
# `.agents/` is deliberately NOT ignored wholesale. It used to be, and the skills under
# `.agents/skills/` are committed, so the rule shadowed ten tracked files and would have
# swallowed the next one added beside them — the exact trap the worker-binary block above
# describes, in the other direction. Local state directly under `.agents/` stays ignored;
# the tracked subtree is re-admitted because excluding a directory stops git descending
# into it at all, so `.agents/*` alone would still hide the skills.
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/*
!.agents/skills/
skills-lock.json

# Spec Kit — local-only (not part of the freehire tree). Keep on disk for personal
# workflows; never commit tooling, constitution memory, or generated feature specs.
.specify/
# Ignore Cursor local state; keep shared agent rules in the tree.
.cursor/*
!.cursor/rules/
!.cursor/rules/**
/specs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Superpowers visual brainstorm scratch
.superpowers/

# Agent scratch: review reports, local run logs, throwaway seed SQL. Deliberately
# outside git — it is a working directory, not an artifact, and a `git add -A` had
# already swept a server log and a local seed script into a commit before this line
# existed.
.cache/

# Node / Vite / Vitest caches. The frontend lives in web/ with its own
# .gitignore; these guard against a stray tool run (e.g. vitest) from the repo
# root leaking a node_modules/.vite cache into the Go project.
node_modules/
.vite/
.svelte-kit/

# extension/ (WXT + Svelte browser extension) generated dirs and release zips
extension/.wxt/
extension/.output/
extension/*.zip

# Local-only compose overrides (per-machine service wiring; never shared).
/docker-compose.override.yml

# Go / Vitest coverage profiles and HTML (make cover, pnpm test:coverage).
/coverage/
/web/coverage/

# Playwright e2e run artifacts (pnpm --dir web run test:e2e).
/web/test-results/
.pnpm-store/
.tmp-containers/

# The model bake-off's profile fixtures: a real CV, a real experience bank. This repository
# is public and a CV is a name, a phone number, an address and an employment history, so
# they stay local and are rebuilt from the account they belong to. The postings the bake-off
# runs against ARE committed — they are already public.
#
# The pattern is a PREFIX, not two filenames. Naming each file meant the second one
# (bakeoff-resume.json) landed untracked-but-visible until somebody noticed, and the next
# one would too. See internal/api/handler/assistant_bakeoff.go.
/internal/api/handler/testdata/bakeoff-profile*.json
/internal/api/handler/testdata/bakeoff-resume*.json

# Local Talent Network demo data (see the catalogue AGENTS.md); not part of the change.
/seed-talent.sql

# scripts/harvest_boards.py / discover_boards.py --write output: per-provider seed JSON for
# cmd/harvest-boards, regenerated from the live boards table + whatever aggregator/query ran.
# Not the catalog's own record (that's `boards`, written by cmd/harvest-boards --apply).
/scripts/.harvest-seeds/

# Local research notes (competitor scans, market notes) — kept out of the repository.
/docs/research/
.schemathesis/
